{"kind": "TaskSpecFrozen", "mission_id": "northstar_0c_pit_evidence_gateway_research_store", "recorded_at": "2026-08-17T03:11:54.195662+00:00", "session_id": "ns0c-research-store-foundation-003", "task_id": "ns0c-rs-t1", "taskspec": {"acceptance_criteria": ["RS1 persists a lossless canonical representation reproducing EvidenceSnapshot.from_json without changing snapshot_id, payload_hash, PIT, provenance, supersedes_snapshot_id or payload", "RS2 immutable: identical canonical bytes are idempotent success; different bytes under the same snapshot identity FAIL CLOSED; evidence is never overwritten in place", "RS3 every read reconstructs through canonical contract validation, never an unchecked dict treated as trusted evidence", "RS4 exact snapshot_id lookup with explicit FOUND / NOT_FOUND / REFUSED outcomes; missing evidence is never an empty successful artifact", "RS5 EvidenceRef lookup where the returned snapshot satisfies ref.matches(snapshot); wrong or mismatched refs fail closed", "RS6 deterministic corpus query over source_id, entity_id, entity_type, evidence_type with stable order independent of insertion order", "RS7 no API silently chooses latest, current, authoritative or best among multiple matches", "RS8 a snapshot and its revision coexist; independent sources coexist; uniqueness is canonical snapshot identity, never entity/type/period/source", "RS9 storage does not claim historical admissibility; future evidence may be stored today", "RS10 the stored corpus routes through the gateway for historical reads; PIT logic is not duplicated in the store", "RS11 tampered, hash-mismatched, identity-mismatched and malformed records do not reconstruct as valid evidence", "RS12 reopen in a fresh process reproduces identical canonical identity with no process memory", "RS13 the same query after reopen returns the same ordered identities", "RS14 no canonical 0B contract semantics change; a required change means STOP and ESCALATE", "RS15 no production mutation, capital action, vendor commitment, authority promotion, C1 activation or Phase 0D work"], "base_sha": "9b1e04381ef0bce6e4bd9d5d9347fb3988045e67", "escalation_conditions": ["a canonical 0B contract change appears necessary -> STOP, ESCALATE", "a requirement cannot be met without deciding winner policy or effective_period -> ABSTAIN", "durable review infrastructure cannot initialise -> remain UNVERIFIED and STOP"], "executor": "CLAUDE", "forbidden_operations": ["MODIFY_0B_CANONICAL_CONTRACTS", "HISTORICAL_AS_OF_API", "LOOKAHEAD_AUDIT", "WINNER_POLICY_DECISION", "EFFECTIVE_PERIOD_DECISION", "VECTOR_SEARCH", "SEMANTIC_SEARCH", "RANKING", "EXTERNAL_DATABASE", "VENDOR_INTEGRATION", "PRODUCTION_WIRING", "AUTHORITY_CHANGE", "C1_ACTIVATION", "PHASE_0D", "MERGE", "DEPLOY"], "goal": "Durable, immutable persistence of canonical EvidenceSnapshot objects with exact identity/reference retrieval and deterministic metadata corpus query. Storage and corpus retrieval ONLY: historical admissibility stays with the EvidenceGateway, revision winner selection stays unresolved, and effective_period stays undecided.", "known_tensions_recorded_at_freeze": ["RS2 vs re-acquisition: the same facts fetched twice yield the SAME snapshot_id with DIFFERENT bytes, because retrieved_at and provenance.recorded_at are excluded from identity. RS2 is frozen and says FAIL CLOSED, so a re-acquisition carrying a fresh retrieved_at is REFUSED rather than silently deduplicated or silently overwritten. This is deliberate: the store cannot pick between two acquisition envelopes without inventing a policy, and silently discarding one would rewrite acquisition history. Recorded here at freeze time rather than discovered later; whether ingestion should reuse stored bytes on re-fetch is an operator question for the next task, NOT a licence to soften this criterion after seeing results."], "max_attempts": 2, "mission_id": "northstar_0c_pit_evidence_gateway_research_store", "protected_paths": ["portfolio_automation/northstar/", "config/", ".agent/", "docs/NORTHSTAR_0C_SESSION_ns0c-evgw-foundation-001.jsonl", "docs/NORTHSTAR_0C_SESSION_ns0c-revision-supersession-002.jsonl"], "risk_class": "E3_HIGH", "storage_backend": "stdlib sqlite3", "task_id": "ns0c-rs-t1", "title": "Research Store Foundation", "verification_steps": ["focused tests during implementation", "full relevant set before certification", "ONE final SERIAL broad regression; baseline captured serially at 9b1e0438", "exact failure node identities persisted; NEW_RELEVANT_FAILURES = 0"]}, "taskspec_hash": "sha256:190edebc3dc5c0182ed9cead707707b316b24171f4796cd0ed781762036b6df8"}
